# Your Finance, Sales, and Inventory Systems Don't Match

Different departments run on different systems, so numbers never quite reconcile.

When finance, sales, and inventory each run their own disconnected system, the same order can show different statuses in different places, and month-end reconciliation becomes a manual, error-prone exercise in comparing exports.

Symptoms:
- Inventory counts that don't match what sales or finance see
- Manual, spreadsheet-based month-end reconciliation
- Delayed visibility into which orders are actually fulfilled versus billed
- Departments each trusting their own numbers over anyone else's

Our solution: We implement or integrate an ERP that gives finance, sales, and inventory one shared source of truth, with real-time sync instead of periodic exports, so every department is working from the same numbers.

FAQs:

Q: Do we need to replace all our existing systems?
A: Often not. ERP integration can connect existing tools rather than requiring a full replacement, depending on how outdated the current systems are.

Q: How disruptive is an ERP rollout?
A: A phased approach, starting with the highest-friction reconciliation point, minimizes disruption compared to a single big-bang cutover.